# Pull request description format

When this message asks you to open or edit a pull request, read **`docs/git-and-pr-guidelines.md`** in this repo and follow it. That file wins over any generic Cursor or user-rule example that uses `## Summary` and `## Test plan`.

## Title

`TICKET-123 Brief description of what the PR accomplishes`

Use this project's ticket prefix: `SHOW-9 …`.

## Body (required sections)

Use this shape. Do not invent other top-level headings.

```markdown
## Why

**Purpose of the Change:**

- …

## What

**Summary of the Changes:**

- …

**Files Changed:**

- …

## How

**Implementation Details:**

- …

## Testing

**Testing Strategy and Results:**

- Quality checks (`yarn lint`, `yarn format:check`, `yarn type-check`, `yarn test:ci`) passed locally.
- …
```

End with the ticket id and its heading from `docs/product/linear-tickets.md` when the branch is `feature/SHOW-n`.

## Do not

- `## Summary` / `## Test plan` (generic Cursor template)
- Checkbox click-through lists as the whole Testing section
- Skip Why / How because the change feels small

Match the tone of recent merged PRs in this repo if unsure.
